			"date": "2024-03-05T23:27:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>Well that turned into the inevitable SEO rabbit hole!  </p><p>So, of course it depends...</p><p><a href=\"https://www.seroundtable.com/google-core-web-vitals-priority-34937.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">seroundtable.com/google-core-w</span><span class=\"invisible\">eb-vitals-priority-34937.html</span></a></p><p>But then I found older articles where John has said it is a ranking factor - but could not find where he has recently said not that big of one though. (SEO can be so hard.)<br> <br>I think I was wrong to say it was only a deciding factor - a lot depends on what's going on with a sites's complexity and how it delivers to the user.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
